:option {:value "255809"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255822"} "Kayak Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255835"} "Kayak Fours, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255848"} "Canadian Singles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255861"} "Canadian Singles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255873"} "Canadian Doubles, 500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255886"} "Canadian Doubles, 1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "255897"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "255907"} "Kayak Doubles, 500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "255919"} "Kayak Fours, 500 metres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "255441"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "255581"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "255675"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "255925"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "256068"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "256204"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "256317"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258743"} "2008"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/159"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Kayak Singles, 500 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "26 – 30 September 1988"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/640"} "Mi-sa-ri Jo-jeong-gyeong-gi-jang, Hanam"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/255783"} "18 from 18 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The men’s K-1 500 results at the last three editions of the World Championships had been inconsistent and thus there were no clear favorites in the event, with the three victors having been East Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9851"} "Andreas Stähle"] ", New Zealand’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10436"} "Paul MacDonald"] ", and Great Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9789"} "Jeremy West"] ". MacDonald was a 1984 Olympic champion in the K-2 500 and the K-4 1000, but he had accomplished these feats in the absence of most of the major canoeing nations due to the Soviet-led boycott. Stähle, meanwhile, was the only competitor at the last three World Championships to have taken home more than one medal in the event, as he was also the 1987 runner-up."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Stähle won his heat in the opening round, but it was Hungary’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10061"} "Zsolt Gyulay"] ", the 1986 World runner-up, who set an Olympic record, defeating MacDonald and helping to relegate West to the repêchage in the process. Gyulay again eliminated West and posted the fastest time in the semi-finals, while Stähle came in third behind MacDonald and Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10805"} "Karl Sundqvist"] " as " [:a {:href "/athletes/11006"} "Viktor Pusev"] " of the Soviet Union took the third heat. Gyulay took the gold medal with ease, but the remainder of the race was an exciting battle where almost every competitor was in contention for the remaining podium spots as they approached the finish line. Stähle, MacDonald, America’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/11098"} "Mike Herbert"] ", Sundqvist, and Czechoslovakia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/10728"} "Attila Szabó"] ", the 1987 World runner-up, crossed in that order with only a second between them, and even last-placed Pusev was less than two and a half seconds behind Stähle. Each of the podium finishers in this event went on to win multiple medals in Seoul:  Gyulay became a double Olympic champion with a victory in the K-4 1000, Stähle captured bronze in the same event, and MacDonald won the K-2 500 and was runner-up in the K-2 1000."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Rep"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "265"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10061"} "Zsolt Gyulay"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "1:41.24 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:41.52 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:44.82 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "244"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9851"} "Andreas Stähle"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "1:44.26 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:45.51 (3 h2)"] [:td {} "1:46.38 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "328"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10436"} "Paul MacDonald"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "1:41.65 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "1:43.33 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:46.46 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "406"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11098"} "Mike Herbert"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:43.41 (4 h1)"] [:td {} "– (AC h1)"] [:td {} "1:43.40 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:46.73 (4)"] [:td {}] [:td {